          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Show that for any non-zero real value of ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "k",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", the following quadratic equations can ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "never",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " have real roots.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q9a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2-2kx+3k^2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Delta=-8k^2<0$ for $k\\ne0$, so there are no real roots.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-2k)^2-4(1)(3k^2)\\\\\\Delta&=4k^2-12k^2\\\\\\Delta&=-8k^2\\end{align*}$$\nFor non-zero real $k$, $k^2>0$. Thus $\\Delta<0$ and there are no real roots.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q9b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2+2x+1+k^2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Delta=-4k^2<0$ for $k\\ne0$, so there are no real roots.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=2^2-4(1)(1+k^2)\\\\\\Delta&=4-4-4k^2\\\\\\Delta&=-4k^2\\end{align*}$$\nFor non-zero real $k$, $k^2>0$. Thus $\\Delta<0$ and there are no real roots.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q9c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$kx-5k^2=x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Delta=-19k^2<0$ for $k\\ne0$, so there are no real roots.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-kx+5k^2&=0\\\\\\Delta&=(-k)^2-4(1)(5k^2)\\\\\\Delta&=k^2-20k^2\\\\\\Delta&=-19k^2\\end{align*}$$\nFor non-zero real $k$, $k^2>0$. Thus $\\Delta<0$ and there are no real roots.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q9d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x^2+2kx+2k^2+k+1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Delta=-4\\left(k+\\frac12\\right)^2-3<0$, so there are no real roots.\n\nComplete the square in the discriminant.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(2k)^2-4(1)(2k^2+k+1)\\\\\\Delta&=-4(k^2+k+1)\\\\\\Delta&=-4\\left[\\left(k+\\frac12\\right)^2+\\frac34\\right]\\\\\\Delta&=-4\\left(k+\\frac12\\right)^2-3\\end{align*}$$\nThe square is non-negative, so $\\Delta\\le-3<0$. Hence there are no real roots for any non-zero real $k$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
  },
